		<h2>3. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
		<h3>Does a battery eliminate grid reliance completely?</h3>
		<p>No. A home battery is sized to offset peak evening hours (typically 4 PM to 9 PM). Complete off-grid independence requires larger battery capacity and generator integration.</p>

		<h2>4. Sources & Calculation Methodology</h2>
		<p class="sources-text">Data derived from CPUC Net Billing Tariff Decision D.22-12-056 and public utility rate schedules for PG&E, SCE, and SDG&E. All payback calculations assume a 30% Federal Tax Credit eligibility and regional baseline utility inflation rates.</p>

